= Core fixture and generated evidence integration

This bounded investigation reconciles two independently approved preparations
onto the approved core test-inference head. The runtime-facing change adds only
#raw("benchmarks/performance/gg-hhh-topology.toml") to the existing
#raw("gammaloop-api") compile-time test-source owner. The 851-byte fixture is
unchanged. The documentation change installs the approved generated-evidence
owner, its manifest, and the already-locked #raw("sha2 0.10.9") dependency edge.
No production algorithm, numerical expectation, kernel, test policy, worker
limit, timeout, NixCI setting, vendor source, or physics asset changes.

The final Git-pinned core producer is newly realized because the dependency and
source-selection edges change its derivation. Its canonical fast selection
passes 2,214 top-level tests: 451 #raw("gammaloop-api"), 19 tracing-filter,
1,587 #raw("gammalooprs"), and 157 three-dimensional-representation tests.
Nineteen Rust tests are ignored and sixteen existing tests are excluded by the
default filter; neither class receives pass credit. The seven stale parser
selector names have no matching test in the archive inventory and receive no
execution or skip credit. A separate exact selection passes the topology-card
boundary test once.

The final code also passes 116 docs-builder library tests, the canonical builder
check, all 110 authoritative developer-scope digests, formatting, scoped Clippy,
Hakari, feature isolation, and the CI graph check. The Git-pinned docs-pages
source is evaluated rather than published. With an empty #raw("PATH"), its
metadata-free prose/evidence boundary accepts the qualified source and rejects a
task-owned copy containing one unauthorized HTML file. The eight historical
rendered HTML artifacts and all twenty-five declared source, receipt, and tool
bindings are preserved; ignored review scratch is excluded by repository
membership rather than deletion.

This is an integration record, not a broad documentation-owner approval. The
81 oracle-row failures and the other accepted WP3 obligations remain open. No
full-site output, distribution, performance, memory, M-rebuild, or WP3
completion is claimed. Evidence and immutable preparation approvals are bound
by #link("evidence/generation-integration/wp3/core-docs/receipt.json")[the
combined receipt]. A NEW independent combined review is required before any QED
migration or later WP3 step.
